# sound-theme-freedesktop -- the sounds themselves.
#
# WITHOUT THIS, LIBCANBERRA IS SILENT AND NOTHING SAYS SO. libcanberra is a
# player; this is what it plays. With libcanberra, libvorbis, libogg and libtool
# all installed and mutter built -Dsound_player=true, a system with no sound
# theme produces no sound at all -- and no build check anywhere covers the join,
# because the player and the theme are separate packages that never reference
# each other at build time. Identical shape to the JXL wallpapers needing
# libjxl's loader, the SVG icons needing librsvg's, and xkbcomp being a runtime
# dependency the X server shells out to.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://people.freedesktop.org/~mccann/dist/sound-theme-freedesktop-0.8.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=cb518b20eef05ec2e82dda1fa89a292c1760dc023aba91b8aa69bafac85e8a14
SRC_DIR=sound-theme-freedesktop-0.8

# Pure data -- 27 Ogg Vorbis files and a text file, nothing compiled -- so it is
# built once and installed everywhere, exactly like gnome-backgrounds. PKG_ARCH
# is read from this file by CI's select job AND by the Makefile's pkg_target, so
# this single line is the whole declaration; the two used to be separate and a
# recipe declaring only one produced an "any" package locally and two
# arch-stamped ones in CI, with nothing to say so.
PKG_ARCH=any

# THIS RECIPE DOES NOT USE UPSTREAM'S BUILD SYSTEM, DELIBERATELY, AND THAT IS A
# REAL DIVERGENCE RATHER THAN A SHORTCUT.
#
# The package is pure data: 27 stereo .oga files and one six-line index.theme.
# Nothing is compiled. But its configure.ac:13 is IT_PROG_INTLTOOL([0.40.0]) and
# its Makefile.am:14 runs $(INTLTOOL_MERGE), so building it the upstream way
# requires intltool -- which requires XML::Parser -- and NEITHER IS PACKAGED
# HERE. Both are LFS chapter 8 packages, which is again why BLFS lists no
# dependencies for this package at all.
#
# What those two packages would buy is this file, in its entirety:
#
#     [Sound Theme]
#     _Name=Default
#     Directories=stereo
#
#     [stereo]
#     OutputProfile=stereo
#
# One translatable key. AND THE TARBALL SHIPS ZERO .po FILES -- so intltool-merge
# has nothing to merge, and its whole effect is to strip the leading underscore
# from _Name. Two packages, one of them a perl XML module, to remove one
# underscore from one line.
#
# So build.sh does nothing and install.sh lays the tree down directly. The cost
# of that choice is drift: we hand-write a file upstream generates, and if
# index.theme.in ever grows real content our copy silently stops matching.
# install.sh therefore CHECKS ITS OWN OUTPUT AGAINST index.theme.in key by key
# and fails on any key it does not know -- which turns that drift from silent
# into loud. That check is the price of skipping the build system and must not
# be removed with it.
#
# This does not foreclose packaging intltool later. If a package in this tier
# genuinely needs it, it gets packaged then at exactly today's cost, and this
# recipe stays a data package regardless -- nothing about it improves by
# retrofitting a build system that strips one underscore.
